==Battleground==
*2 [[Sir Seal]]s spawn, delay 6.67~13.33 seconds<sup>200f~400f</sup>.
*1 [[St. Pigge the 2nd]] spawns after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
*3 [[Sir Seal]]s spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 3.33~10 seconds<sup>100f~300f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Wondermaria (Enemy)|Wondermaria]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn, delay 20~30 seconds<sup>600f~900f</sup>.
**8 [[Shadow Boxer K]]s spawn, delay 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
**4 [[Shy Boy]]s spawn, delay 30~33.33 seconds<sup>900f~1,000f</sup>.
**1 [[Dark Emperor Nyandam]] spawns.

==Strategy==
The start-off is extremely generous with 5 very profitable Sir-Seals spawning with no other support besides an also profitable St. Pigge, so stalling all of them, especially with [[Double Bounty]] units like [[Can Can Cat]], can easily max out the wallet, although even just the first two will often give enough money to deal with the following enemies.

The initial pressure is just the Nyandam, two pushers in the form of a Shy Boy and a Shadow Boxer, and Wondermaria, who is very fast, allowing her to be lured slightly to isolate her from the backline threat. However, her [[Knockback]] abilities and wide attack area allow her to push forward easily, so she should still be kept away from the base. Even short-ranged units like Can Can or [[Bullet Train Cat]] if they were the bounty unit of choice can get some hits in here.

[[Anti-Floating Cats]] like [[Sanzo Cat]] and [[Octopus Cat]] can crowd control and tank the Floating enemies enough to let you focus on the [[Dark Enemies]], who can be controlled but are best killed quickly instead, as standard options like [[Bombercat]] are difficult to use given the boss, and they will give more money anyways. There are two main choices for attackers: fast ones like [[Fishman Cat]] or [[Awakened Bahamut Cat]] who can rush in through the boss's knockbacks and even rebound off of them for extra damage, or units that outrange the boss entirely, with the first category being most helpful if attempting to kill the boss before more support arrives.

The flow of meatshields can be intentionally interrupted to allow the boss to hit backliners, as while this will damage them, the knockback can save them from even greater damage from the supporting enemies.

